// tools/delete-test -- P1 Item 2 proof harness for ACCOUNT DELETION (cscript
// JScript) over the REAL BYTES of js/state.js + js/integrations.js, loaded in one
// scope with a scripted Firebase stub and a minimal synchronous Promise shim.
// EXTENSIONLESS on purpose (see tools/parse-check).
//
// Usage:  cscript //nologo //E:jscript tools/delete-test
// Exit:   0 = every case passed · 1 = a case failed · 2 = could not load
//
// Proves the RULED ORDER and every failure leg of deleteAccount:
//   [A] re-auth refused        -> NOTHING deleted (cloud or local), session live, phase 'reauth'
//   [B] batch commit fails     -> NOTHING deleted, nothing local touched, phase 'firestore'
//   [C] Auth delete fails AFTER the batch -> cloud gone, LOCAL INTACT, praxis_user intact,
//                                 phase 'auth', recoverable:true (the account syncs back up)
//   [D] success                -> phases reauth -> cloud -> login -> local; the batch held
//                                 every collection under the uid (8 private + aiUsage +
//                                 publicProfiles + publishedArcs by authorUid + follows by
//                                 BOTH endpoints + buildOns by fromUid); Auth user deleted;
//                                 every localStorage key carrying the uid gone, the global
//                                 caches gone, the OTHER uid's keys untouched; this uid's
//                                 photos deleted per record and the other uid's kept;
//                                 praxis_user null; signed out; status 'deleted'
//   [E] re-run after success   -> idempotent: completes with nothing to delete
//   [F] the local-key sweep    -> accountLocalKeysFor(uid) finds every per-uid key shape
//                                 Items 1/3/4 and the app write, and none of another uid's

